  "category": "Digital/Shift registers",
  "family": "74LS",
  "nominal_temperature_c": 25,
  "model_notes": [
    "Own event-driven functional model; no vendor SPICE source copied. The .casim file contains all device-specific behavior.",
    "Package pin numbers, control polarity, functional state and finite nominal delays are represented. Initial storage is unknown until reset, parallel load or enough valid clocks.",
    "Delays are per logic block, not a complete timing-characterization matrix. Allow settling and obey setup/hold; metastability and timing violations are not modeled.",
    "Input thresholds scale with local supply. LS/HCT/AHCT thresholds are calibrated to 0.8/2 V at 5 V; LS outputs approximate 3.4/0.2 V before loading.",
    "Finite output resistance, input capacitance and package quiescent current are fixed approximate nominal parameters. No detailed fan-out, TTL input current, ESD, parasitic power, thermal drift or damage.",
    "Outputs release outside the supply window. No retention through a power cycle is guaranteed.",
    "Physical clock inputs use supply-relative Schmitt action; data and other controls retain 0/X/1 conversion. All-input Schmitt behavior of AHC/AHCT is not reproduced.",
    "No fixed small global maximum timestep; XSPICE schedules internal events. Use circuit resolution appropriate to the electrical stimulus.",
    "PL LOW loads all parallel bits asynchronously. CE HIGH inhibits the clock.",
    "The effective clock is CP OR CE, as in the device clock gate; changing CE from LOW to HIGH while CP is LOW can cause a rising edge. Change CE while CP is HIGH.",
    "Parallel data may change while PL is LOW, with finite gate/load delay; do not use the model to assess load/clock races."
  ]
}
